# Math Checker V5 - environment variable reference (PLACEHOLDERS ONLY)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file is documentation, not configuration. Math Checker does NOT load
# .env files: the variables below are read from the process environment, so set
# them in the shell that launches the app (or in the launcher) before running
# start.bat / python main.py.
#
# Copy nothing sensitive here. API keys, Google OAuth tokens and the database
# password-equivalents belong to the app's own data folder (config.toml and
# secrets.toml, created by the setup wizard under data/ or %LOCALAPPDATA%
# \MathChecker\) and are git-ignored. This repository must never contain a real
# key, token or client secret.
#
# Default behaviour with none of these set is correct for a normal install.

# --- Data location ---------------------------------------------------------
# Folder that holds app.db, config.toml, secrets.toml, logs/ and mark_schemes/.
# Tests and throw-away snapshots set this; nothing overrides it.
# Leave unset to use the checkout's own data/ folder (source checkout) or
# %LOCALAPPDATA%\MathChecker\ (installed copy).
#MC5_DATA_DIR=C:\path\to\a\separate\data\folder

# --- First-run behaviour ---------------------------------------------------
# 1 = synthetic demo data, Classroom disabled, mock AI (no keys needed).
# The UI labels this mode DEMO. Never use it for real marking.
#MC5_DEMO=0

# 1 = do not open a browser window when the backend starts.
#MC5_NO_BROWSER=0

# --- Network / access ------------------------------------------------------
# Port recorded for the supervised / public-access lifecycle (the launcher and
# the relay use it to find the copy that is actually serving). A normal launch
# takes its port from the command line (`python main.py 9000`) or from
# config.toml [network]; an occupied port falls back to a free one.
#MC5_PORT=8642

# 1 = LAN/public mode (see docs/SERVER_LIFECYCLE.md and remote.py). Session
# protection is mandatory in this mode; do not enable it casually.
#MC5_PUBLIC=0

# 1 = require sign-in before any page is served, including on loopback.
#MC5_LOGIN_REQUIRED=0

# Comma-separated extra origins allowed to call the API. Leave empty for the
# built-in loopback origins.
#MC5_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# --- Diagnostics -----------------------------------------------------------
# Level for the distributed-bootstrap log event (default WARNING). The app's own
# log level is configured in Settings, not here.
#MC5_LOG_LEVEL=WARNING

# --- Browser development only (frontend/) ----------------------------------
# The Vite dev server refuses to start without an explicit backend. This is the
# same value as frontend/.env.local; keep it out of production installs.
# See frontend/.env.development.example.
#MC5_DEV_API=http://127.0.0.1:8642
